docs/how-to/set-up-accounts.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard init --force --organization <org> --anthropic-key <key> --github-app-id <app id> --github-installation-id <installation id> --github-private-key-file <path to .pem>
docs/how-to/ship-a-release.md	The run also publishes the images as `ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>` (bot), `-resident` and `-sandbox`, at `:<version>` and `:latest`, with provenance and an SBOM ([Deploy](deploy.md#run-the-container-yourself) verifies one). A third job publishes `@coreplane/switchboard` to npm only for a release cut from the default branch and only while the variable `SWITCHBOARD_PUBLISH_NPM` is `true` — turn it off before merging a release PR and that release ships everything but the package — on the run's own identity — npm trusts this workflow as the package's publisher, so no token is stored anywhere ([Configure the repository](configure-the-repository.md#5-repository-secrets-and-variables)).
docs/reference/specs/init.md	| From an empty directory, `init` with real values followed by the tutorial's Part 1 reaches an answer from `ask`; with `--cloudflare`, Part 3 reaches a live `/healthz` from the written profile (items 1–4, 8, 11) | `[agent]` Follow [Get started](../../tutorials/get-started.md) as written on a machine with nothing set up, in an empty directory: `npx @coreplane/switchboard init --organization <org> --anthropic-key <key>` → `wrote:` lists `.env  (mode 600)` and `config/config.yaml`, `ls -l .env` shows `-rw-------`, `npx @coreplane/switchboard ask "what can you do?"` answers; then `npx @coreplane/switchboard init --force --organization <org> --anthropic-key <key> --cloudflare <account> --zone <zone>` → `deploy/profile.json` and `Worker configs from deploy/profile.json:` with a `written .switchboard/deploy/<worker>/wrangler.jsonc` line per Worker, and the tutorial's Part 3 from `deploy secrets memory` on ends with `curl -sS https://<name>.<zone>/healthz` answering JSON. Human-gated: needs a real key, a Slack workspace and a Cloudflare account. |
docs/reference/cli.md	Not a registered command either — the **bot process** itself, the one the container image runs: Slack over Socket Mode and, with `PORT` set, the HTTP server and the dashboard, until Ctrl-C. It reads `.env` and `config/config.yaml` from the installation (`SWITCHBOARD_HOME`, else the directory you run it in when that holds one, else `~/.switchboard`; a checkout is always its own); `start --help` lists everything it reads. From the published package it is `npx @coreplane/switchboard start` — the bot from an empty directory with no Docker.
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	MEMORY_TOKEN="$(cat ~/.secrets/switchboard/MEMORY_TOKEN)" npx @coreplane/switchboard deploy all --only memory,bot
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard ask "what can you do?"
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard deploy plan --only memory,bot
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard deploy secrets bot
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard deploy secrets memory
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard init --force --organization <org> --anthropic-key <key> --slack-app-token <xapp-token> --slack-bot-token <xoxb-token>
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard init --force --organization <org> --anthropic-key <key> --slack-app-token <xapp-token> --slack-bot-token <xoxb-token> --cloudflare <account id> --zone <zone>
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard init --organization <org> --anthropic-key <key>
docs/tutorials/get-started.md	npx @coreplane/switchboard start
docs/tutorials/run-it-locally.md	`npm run cli --` is the checkout's spelling of the published CLI; the same code ships as `@coreplane/switchboard`.
docs/tutorials/run-it-locally.md	git clone https://github.com/coreplanelabs/switchboard.git

# The npm package is the project under its published name — `npmPackage` in project.json, held equal here by check:project-facts — and its manifest and README name the repository and the image the same way the root's do.
packages/switchboard/package.json	"name": "@coreplane/switchboard",
packages/switchboard/package.json	"url": "git+https://github.com/coreplanelabs/switchboard.git",
packages/switchboard/package.json	"url": "https://github.com/coreplanelabs/switchboard/issues"

# The deploy how-to's operator-directory example runs the package by its published name.

# The smoke test's --cloudflare refusal needs an account id of the real shape (32 hex characters); this is the documented synthetic one, not an account.
packages/switchboard/smoke.test.mts	const account = "0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef";

# `deploy plan` from the example profile prints the example's placeholder account inside each account-registry image reference.

# The package README names the package once.

# The plan snapshots print the example profile's placeholder account (32 zeros), not an account.
src/core/__snapshots__/capabilitySurfaces.test.ts.snap	Images: registry (version 1.2.3) — not probed (the example profile) — bot: registry.cloudflare.com/00000000000000000000000000000000/switchboard:1.2.3
src/core/__snapshots__/capabilitySurfaces.test.ts.snap	Images: registry (version 1.2.3) — not probed (the example profile) — bot: registry.cloudflare.com/00000000000000000000000000000000/switchboard:1.2.3, resident: registry.cloudflare.com/00000000000000000000000000000000/switchboard-resident:1.2.3, sandbox: registry.cloudflare.com/00000000000000000000000000000000/switchboard-sandbox:1.2.3
